---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TrustStrip from '../../components/TrustStrip.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "What does 4 red blinks on a Tesla Wall Connector mean?",
    "answer": "Four red blinks on a Gen 3 Wall Connector typically indicate a ground fault or high resistance at the terminal block. This can be caused by loose wire connections, moisture intrusion, or a faulty internal ground fault sensor."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I install a Tesla Wall Connector on a 50-amp breaker?",
    "answer": "Yes. The Tesla Wall Connector is configurable from 12A to 48A. On a 50-amp breaker with appropriate wire (6 AWG copper), set the unit to 40 amps for code compliance with the 125% continuous load rule."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is Tesla power sharing?",
    "answer": "Power sharing allows two or more Tesla Wall Connectors on the same circuit to dynamically split available current. When one car finishes, the other ramps to full speed. This requires a low-voltage data cable between units."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does the Universal Wall Connector work with non-Tesla vehicles?",
    "answer": "Yes. The Tesla Universal Wall Connector includes an integrated J1772 adapter, charging any electric vehicle that uses the J1772 or NACS (Tesla) connector standard."
  },
  {
    "question": "How much does installation cost?",
    "answer": "Every home has different electrical configurations. We provide transparent on-site assessments where we explain exactly what work is needed based on your panel, wire run distance, and charger model. Call (425) 380-0019 to schedule a visit."
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Tesla Wall Connector Installation & Repair Issaquah | Gen 3 & Universal"
  description="Certified Tesla Wall Connector installation and repair in Issaquah WA. Gen 2, Gen 3, and Universal models. Power sharing setups. Call (425) 380-0019."
  canonicalPath="/services/tesla-wall-connector-installation-repair/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services/' },
    { name: 'Tesla Wall Connector Installation & Repair' }
  ]} />

  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 840px;">
        <span class="section-tag" style="background: rgba(132, 204, 22, 0.2); color: #84cc16;">Specialized EV Service</span>
        <h1>Tesla Wall Connector Installation & Repair in Issaquah, WA</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">From Gen 2 units with hardwired pigtails to Gen 3 Wi-Fi-enabled models and the new Universal Wall Connector with J1772 and NACS compatibility, our electricians install, repair, and configure Tesla charging hardware to factory specifications.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta-wrap">
          <a href="tel:+14253800019" class="btn btn-lime"><span>📞</span><span>Call (425) 380-0019</span></a>
          <a href="/locations/" class="btn btn-outline-white">View All 15 Service Areas</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <TrustStrip />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="rich-content" style="max-width: 900px; margin-inline: auto;">
        <h2>What This Service Covers</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Hardwired 60A circuit installation for 48-amp continuous charging</li>
          <li>Gen 3 Wi-Fi configuration and firmware verification</li>
          <li>Power sharing setup for dual Tesla Wall Connectors</li>
          <li>Thermal sensor diagnostics for red fault indicator codes</li>
          <li>Gen 2 to Gen 3 or Universal upgrades on existing circuits</li>
          <li>Rotary DIP switch amperage configuration for older models</li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/tesla-wall-connector-repair-installation.jpg" 
            alt="Tesla Wall Connector Gen 3 installed on garage wall charging Tesla in Issaquah WA 98029"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Factory-certified Tesla Wall Connector installation configured for 48-amp continuous output on 60-amp branch circuit.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <h2>Technical Background & How It Works</h2>
        <p>The Tesla Wall Connector is one of the most popular home EVSE units in King County. Unlike generic J1772 chargers, Tesla chargers communicate directly with the vehicle over a proprietary protocol, enabling features like scheduled charging, load balancing, and real-time energy monitoring through the Tesla app.</p>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/panel-upgrade-200-amp-circuit-breakers.jpg" 
            alt="Dedicated 60-amp dual-pole breaker for Tesla Wall Connector in 200A service panel Issaquah"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Commercial-grade dual-pole breaker installed with copper conductors rated for continuous duty.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <p>However, incorrect installation is the primary cause of Wall Connector failures. Loose terminal screws, improper wire gauge selection, and incorrect breaker sizing cause thermal shutdowns indicated by repeating red LED blink patterns. Our technicians torque all connections to Tesla-specified inch-pound values using calibrated digital torque wrenches.</p>

        <p>This service is available throughout all 15 Issaquah neighborhoods, including <a href="/locations/issaquah-highlands/">Issaquah Highlands</a>, <a href="/locations/talus/">Talus</a>, <a href="/locations/klahanie/">Klahanie</a>, and <a href="/locations/olde-town-issaquah/">Olde Town Issaquah</a>. Browse our full <a href="/locations/">locations hub</a> to find your area.</p>

        <h2>When to Contact Us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>New Tesla Wall Connector needs professional hardwired installation</li>
          <li>Red blinking fault lights on Gen 3 (1 to 7 red blinks each mean different faults)</li>
          <li>Upgrading from Gen 2 to Universal Wall Connector</li>
          <li>Setting up power sharing between two Wall Connectors</li>
          <li>Wi-Fi connectivity or firmware update issues</li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/modern-issaquah-garage-ev-charger.jpg" 
            alt="Universal Tesla Wall Connector mounted in Issaquah home garage"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Universal Wall Connector provides high-speed charging for native NACS Tesla vehicles and J1772 EVs.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <p>For technical questions about tesla wall connector installation & repair in Issaquah, call our dispatch line directly at <a href="tel:+14253800019">(425) 380-0019</a>. Licensed under <a href="https://apps.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=296-46B" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WAC 296-46B</a> and fully compliant with NEC Article 625 standards.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQAccordion items={faqs} />

  <section class="section" style="background: #ffffff; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title-wrap">
        <span class="section-tag">Related Solutions</span>
        <h2>Related EV Charging Services</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
